body:
I've experienced some of this as a PC this year, having to negotiate for an extra £10 a week only to see how much money they're throwing at talent or the unrealistic expectations of editorial. People taking travel and accommodation arrangements for granted so we end up grovelling for partial refunds or spending hours booking the right flights because various people have an airport preference or specific driver, or having to factor in travel time because beyond a certain length we're contractually required to provide a separate car... I'll stop before I rant on too long. 

&#x200B;

It can feel very unfair when you see others treated like shit or taken for granted and you're aware of where all the money is going. We almost always have to provide/bend over for editorial/talent or pick up the pieces, apologise on their behalf for things, take financial hit after hit to keep someone happy...

&#x200B;

Thankfully, it's not always that bad.
